`actors.get(msg.from)` and `actors.get(msg.to)` (lines 293–294) return `undefined` when the actor key is absent. The immediately following accesses `fromActor.x`, `fromActor.width`, `toActor.x`, and `toActor.width` on line 297–298 will throw a `TypeError` at runtime. Guard both lookups before use:
```ts
const fromActor = actors.get(msg.from);
const toActor = actors.get(msg.to);
if (fromActor === undefined || toActor === undefined) return;
```
